# Implementation Plan - Admin Console Live Network Map

Aapke request ke mutabik hum admin panel par bina Google Maps ka use kiye, ek **OpenStreetMap (Leaflet.js) based dynamic Dark-Themed Map** implement karenge. Yeh map:
1. UP ke poore active bus route graph ko draw karega (Lines).
2. Geocoded Bus Stands ko points ki tarah show karega (Markers).
3. Live buses ko real-time coordinate updates ke sath map par move karega.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Backend API Updates

#### [MODIFY] [admin.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/api/admin.ts)
Add a new endpoint `/monitor/map-data` that aggregates:
- All stops coordinates from the graph stops list.
- All route sequences mapped to lat/lng polylines.
This is called once by the map component on load.

---

### Dependency Installation

#### [INSTALL] Leaflet NPM Packages
Install `leaflet` and `@types/leaflet` in the admin package directory to handle map instance rendering.

---

### Admin Panel Page & Layout

#### [MODIFY] [layout.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/admin/src/app/layout.tsx)
Add Leaflet's standard CSS stylesheet via a CDN link in the HTML `<head>` so map controls and layers render correctly.

#### [NEW] [LiveMap.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/admin/src/components/LiveMap.tsx)
Create an isolated Leaflet Map component:
- Uses a `div` reference to instantiate a Leaflet map.
- Uses **CartoDB Dark Matter** tile layers for a premium black/dark UI theme.
- Draws all stops as small light-grey circular nodes.
- Draws all route paths as semi-transparent thin amber/orange lines.
- Renders active buses as circular icons (green for moving, red for stationary) with rotation corresponding to their GPS heading. Clicking/hovering on a bus shows tooltips with registration and route info.
- Automatically handles Next.js SSR issues by checking for window execution.

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/admin/src/app/page.tsx)
- Add a view selector tab (Toggle button: **Console View** / **Map View**) at the top of the admin console.
- Dynamically import the `LiveMap` component with `ssr: false` so it loads on the client side without throwing hydration mismatch warnings.
- Pass the live `buses` state list directly to the map component so the markers update automatically on every 2-second poll.

